{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_dafa9086d239497a8a836a02","type":"tool_result","content":"7ea095b889 engine: carry the Python end-call module-fact re-carriage as one joined literal\nc169eaeb0b engine the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan: commit the work left uncommitted\n31d5f496e3 engine: hold a one-graph bounded scan's graph in RAM when the ceiling fits it\n522a598a1d engine: the-cpp-frontend-s-extension-set-internal-extract-frontend-r (#239)\n39e829d306 c: observe a bounded read loop's untested post-loop cursor cleanup (#228)\n3770e18382 Claim polkit .rules files and emit the subject-gate sibling-arm observation (#225)\n37c2b9db32 Merge pull request #224 from vyprai/engine-work/javascript-has-no-working-receiver-type-route-for-source-bin\n63543ac013 lowering: type a JavaScript module global from the writes that fill it\nde1f355594 Merge pull request #222 from vyprai/engine-work/the-c-c-frontend-records-a-call-s-arguments-as-compacted-sou\nad350f7023 engine: keep a call_arg_const fact behind the scope that declares its name\ne25e3b434f engine: carry a C constant string's content to the call that reads it\nbb3f8cfcc0 frontend: claim the .twig extension so Twig template output lowers (#223)\nd074b01590 Merge pull request #220 from vyprai/engine-work/rust-presence-facts-stop-at-the-function-rsstructuredcontext\n9c99369cc5 Merge branch 'main' into engine-work/rust-presence-facts-stop-at-the-function-rsstructuredcontext\n8c2edb2e9f Merge pull request #218 from vyprai/engine-work/internal-extract-lowering-lowering-go-resolvetargets-looks-a\n5048465f68 Merge branch 'main' into engine-work/internal-extract-lowering-lowering-go-resolvetargets-looks-a\n94631d9d4b engine: attribute an instanceof narrowing to the checked type's visibility (#221)\nc65afe5c75 engine: no-frontend-claims-the-gsp-extension-so-a-grails-template-fi (#219)\n2f761171d5 engine: attribute a Rust sibling helper's facts to the function that calls it\nb9981018d8 lowering: keep an abstract self-declaration's family reach-only\n21cb8e281c lowering: resolve a self-receiver call additively, keeping the fallback first\n34db830eeb lowering: resolve an implicit-receiver member call through the \"this\" key\n902f756d8d cli: keep the validate-binding issue-kind fixture on a corpus-stable concept (#217)\n8d363dba8e lowering: walk the whole base chain when resolving an inherited method call (#216)\n7a23445709 Merge pull request #215 from vyprai/fix/weakrandom-orphan-worklist\n9b971793be definitions: join crypto.InsufficientEntropy to the orphan work list for its four consumer languages\nfd4274b37c Merge pull request #214 from vyprai/engine-work/taint-is-not-routed-into-a-named-function-passed-as-a-callba\n6454c826b5 Merge branch 'main' into engine-work/taint-is-not-routed-into-a-named-function-passed-as-a-callba\n0227dc1d3a Merge pull request #213 from vyprai/engine-work/taint-is-not-followed-through-the-python-locals-builtin-so-a\n8e20e6e269 Merge branch 'main' into engine-work/taint-is-not-followed-through-the-python-locals-builtin-so-a\n---\ncommit 31d5f496e3978c99ed91893c6cc388735759fe90\nAuthor: vyql bot <vyql.bot@vyprsec.ai>\nDate:   Wed Sep 16 23:10:22 2026 +0000\n\n    engine: hold a one-graph bounded scan's graph in RAM when the ceiling fits it\n    \n    -max-ram armed the disk-backed BadgerGraph store for every scan it\n    bounded. For a target whose graph fits in the ceiling, the store costs\n    more than the graph it spares: its detail buffer, write path and caches\n    sit resident alongside a structural core that never leaves RAM in\n    either store, so a multi-package repository that lowers to a\n    million-odd nodes peaked several times its in-RAM footprint (measured\n    4626MiB through the disk store against 1220MiB in RAM on the same\n    repository) and the memory safety stop ended the scan before the first\n    rule ran — an empty report from a 4GB ceiling the scan easily afforded.\n    \n    The partition planner's own affordability measure now decides the\n    store: a target PlanPartitions leaves unpartitioned is a target one\n    graph holds, and that graph is built on the int-indexed in-RAM store —\n    the same store a partitioned scan already builds per partition. A\n    graph the ceiling cannot hold still spills: a target over the\n    one-graph limit is partitioned, and a run that must serialise one\n    graph (-stats, graph-json with review flags) keeps the disk-backed\n    bound. Unbounded scans are untouched; a scan whose cache directories\n    are unwritable keeps its existing in-RAM fallback.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n CHANGELOG.md            | 23 +++++++++++++++++\n cmd/vyql/main.go        | 41 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++---\n cmd/vyql/maxram_test.go | 66 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 3 files changed, 126 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d3b39ce-4baf-4531-a837-11deefe45eb7","uuid":"77f90733-367a-43cc-adf4-87a786200c45","timestamp":"2026-09-19T05:11:55.603Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"7ea095b889 engine: carry the Python end-call module-fact re-carriage as one joined literal\nc169eaeb0b engine the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan: commit the work left uncommitted\n31d5f496e3 engine: hold a one-graph bounded scan's graph in RAM when the ceiling fits it\n522a598a1d engine: the-cpp-frontend-s-extension-set-internal-extract-frontend-r (#239)\n39e829d306 c: observe a bounded read loop's untested post-loop cursor cleanup (#228)\n3770e18382 Claim polkit .rules files and emit the subject-gate sibling-arm observation (#225)\n37c2b9db32 Merge pull request #224 from vyprai/engine-work/javascript-has-no-working-receiver-type-route-for-source-bin\n63543ac013 lowering: type a JavaScript module global from the writes that fill it\nde1f355594 Merge pull request #222 from vyprai/engine-work/the-c-c-frontend-re