ed\n    scan has already executed.\n    \n    analysis.string_scan.missing_length_bound pairs the two halves from the\n=== f71f7be22a\ncommit f71f7be22a319fa94ccbd1dc713276fb91d6fac5\nAuthor: Kiki Luqman Hakiem <4023108+kikihakiem@users.noreply.github.com>\nDate:   Thu Sep 17 19:41:38 2026 +0700\n\n    engine: taint-is-not-traced-into-a-variadic-c-function-call-so-a-pri (#233)\n    \n    * c: trace a variadic call's tail arguments into the wrapper that reads them\n    \n    A C function declares its variadic tail as `...`, which has no parameter\n    name, so the arguments a call passed beyond the named parameters bound to\n    nothing: they kept only the conservative argument-to-result edge, which\n    never enters the callee. A printf-style logging wrapper is exactly that\n    shape and returns void, so every route from a caller's data to the\n    wrapper's own body — where the v-formatted output call lives — was dark,\n    and no definition could name a flow through it (rank 3007, the AIDE\n    control-character log output, CVE-2025-54389).\n    \n    The tail is now modelled the way the JavaScript frontend models\n    `arguments`. A definition that declares `...` and opens a va_list over it\n    gains a synthetic last parameter, __varargs__; the lowering binds every","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
