{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202609191329330c851e412c5c433c","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is the smoking gun for the design:\n\n```sql\nquery pattern callExpr where callee.analysis == \"function.context.end\"\n    and containsAny(args.any.literal, [\"module_call_path:base64.b64encode\", ...])\n    and args.any.literal contains \"module_literal:user_token\"\n```\n\nBindings that read MODULE facts (`module_call_path:`, `module_literal:`, `module_selector:`) anchor with `callee.analysis == \"function.context.end\"` — THE END CALL. That's why the module tokens ride the end call: the bindings that read them QUERY the end call. (`module_literal:user_token` — wait, that's a module TOKEN (`module_literal:` prefix from the structured walk's `literal:` kind), not the raw literal context. Right: moduleTokens come from pyStructuredContextTokens with kinds literal:, call_path:, identifier: etc., prefixed module_. The moduleContext (raw joined literals, no prefix) is a different surface.)\n\nSo who reads the RAW moduleContext (the joined literal text without module_ prefix)? Search bindings for val needles over .context/.source/.sink calls... The raw literals appear in str_args as bare text. A binding anchored on function.context with `args.any.literal contains \"some text\"` would match function-body literals AND module-literal-context AND bodyText. The design intent of carrying moduleContext on the FUNCTION calls: let a function-anchored query see module-level string literals (e.g., a SQL string or a secret defined at module scope near the function).\n\nLet me find Python bindings anchored on function.context / function.context.source / function.context.sink (not .end) that use args.any.literal — those are the surfaces at risk if I move moduleContext to end-only.","signature":"5c1898a05e824958a42250e0"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d3b39ce-4baf-4531-a837-11deefe45eb7","uuid":"2ee16259-8d3a-49d9-b00e-b90ce1132c4b","timestamp":"2026-09-19T05:29:42.222Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202609191329330c851e412c5c433c","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The bindings that read `module_*` facts anchor on `callee.analysis == \"function.context.end\"` — the end call. Now: which bindings anchor on the *other* context calls and read raw literals (the surface at risk if moduleContext moves to end-only)?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d3b39ce-4baf-4531-a837-11deefe45eb7","uuid":"29c65655-497b-421d-8716-1ec9986e8450","timestamp":"2026-09-19T05:29:42.225Z"}
