{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260919134037e554a401eb794f33","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait — one issue with the bound test: `lateMarker` falls out of the prefix... but the LATE literal ALSO becomes a module TOKEN (`module_literal:zz_late_module_literal_zz` — via the structured token walk, capped at 512 TOKENS — my module has ~200 CONST_i literals + markers + function tokens ≈ 210 tokens < 512, so the late marker IS in the tokens!) — and `module_literal:zz_late_module_literal_zz` CONTAINS the substring `zz_late_module_literal_zz` → `strings.Contains(args, lateMarker)` TRUE via the tokens! Bad test design.\n\nFix: assert on the raw literal differently — check the 1024-x fill: `strings.Count(args, strings.Repeat(\"x\",1024))` ≤ 64ish? The raw prefix would contain up to ~63 of the 1KB xxx strings (64KB budget), tokens contain `module_literal:` + first 160 compacted chars of each literal → each CONST_i token contains 160 x's!! Ugh — pyContextValue caps at 160 compact bytes → token = ~160 x's per literal. So counting \"xxxx…\" runs is muddy too.\n\nCleaner: make the late literal something that does NOT become a token: a literal LONGER than 160 bytes never becomes a `module_literal:` token (pyContextValue → pyContextCompact(160) returns \"\" for >160 → no token). So:\n- earlyMarker: short (<160) — appears in raw prefix AND token. Fine (asserting presence).\n- The 200 × 1KB fillers: >160 → no tokens; only in raw context. Count occurrences of the 1KB fill in str_args: bounded prefix keeps ≤ 64 of them. Assert count ≤ 64 (base: 200).\n- lateMarker: make IT also >160B (marker + 200 y's) → no token; assert ABSENT entirely.\n\nLet me rewrite the test accordingly.","signature":"ccace74e269b42c0b1b51e23"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d3b39ce-4baf-4531-a837-11deefe45eb7","uuid":"5ef94a76-109d-48d9-9cb4-7cc58136a585","timestamp":"2026-09-19T05:40:47.881Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260919134037e554a401eb794f33","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The late marker would leak through the *token* surface (`module_literal:` tokens keep ≤160-byte literals). Literals over 160 bytes contribute no token, so make the late marker long — it can then only ride the raw context:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d3b39ce-4baf-4531-a837-11deefe45eb7","uuid":"e74b3c51-3173-4212-a125-8910f6d9bc7f","timestamp":"2026-09-19T05:40:48.705Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260919134037e554a401eb794f33","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_e4bd7e2cdfdb4bdbb8c0b5e2","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/campaign/work/engine-the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan/internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/python_context_economy_test.go","old_string":"func TestPythonModuleLiteralContextIsBounded(t *testing.T) {\n\tconst earlyMarker = \"zz_early_module_literal_zz\"\n\tconst lateMarker = \"zz_late_module_literal_zz\"\n\tvar src bytes.Buffer\n\tfmt.Fprintf(&src, \"EARLY = %q\\n\", earlyMarker)\n\t// ~200KB of literal mass: well past the 64KB bound, reached before the late\n\t// marker, which must fall out of the prefix.\n\tfor i := 0; i < 200; i++ {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(&src, \"CONST_%d = %q\\n\", i, strings.Repeat(\"x\", 1024))\n\t}\n\tfmt.Fprintf(&src, \"LATE = %q\\n\\ndef handler(request):\\n    return request.get('field')\\n\", lateMarker)\n\t_, g := extractAndLowerPython(t, \"fat.py\", src.String())\n\tnodes, err := g.AllNodes()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tendCalls, withEarly, withLate := 0, 0, 0\n\tfor _, n := range nodes {\n\t\tif n.Type != \"code.Call\" || n.Prop(\"callee_path\") != \"analysis.function.context.end\" {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tendCalls++\n\t\targs := n.Prop(\"str_args\")\n\t\tif len(args) > pyModuleLiteralMaxBytes+pyContextBaseTokenLimit*64 {\n\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"end call str_args is %d bytes; the module literal context must be bounded at %d\", len(args), pyModuleLiteralMaxBytes)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif strings.Contains(args, earlyMarker) {\n\t\t\twithEarly++\n\t\t}\n\t\tif strings.Contains(args, lateMarker) {\n\t\t\twithLate++\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif endCalls == 0 {\n\t\tt.Fatal(\"no analysis.function.context.end call was lowered\")\n\t}\n\tif withEarly != endCalls {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the earliest module literal is missing from %d of %d end calls; the bound keeps a prefix, not a sample\", endCalls-withEarly, endCalls)\n\t}\n\tif withLate != 0 {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the module literal context past the bound rides %d of %d end calls; a %d-byte literal mass must not ride every function\", withLate, endCalls, pyModuleLiteralMaxBytes)\n\t}\n}","new_string":"func TestPythonModuleLiteralContextIsBounded(t *testing.T) {\n\tconst earlyMarker = \"zz_early_module_literal_zz\"\n\t// The fill and the late marker are longer than pyContextCompact's 160-byte\n\t// token bound, so they contribute no module_literal: token — the only surface\n\t// they can ride is the raw literal context this case bounds.\n\tfill := strings.Repeat(\"x\", 1024)\n\tlateMarker := \"zz_late_\" + strings.Repeat(\"y\", 256)\n\tvar src bytes.Buffer\n\tfmt.Fprintf(&src, \"EARLY = %q\\n\", earlyMarker)\n\t// ~200KB of literal mass: well past the 64KB bound, reached before the late\n\t// marker, which must fall out of the prefix.\n\tfor i := 0; i < 200; i++ {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(&src, \"CONST_%d = %q\\n\", i, fill)\n\t}\n\tfmt.Fprintf(&src, \"LATE = %q\\n\\ndef handler(request):\\n    return request.get('field')\\n\", lateMarker)\n\t_, g := extractAndLowerPython(t, \"fat.py\", src.String())\n\tnodes, err := g.AllNodes()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tendCalls, withEarly, withLate := 0, 0, 0\n\tfor _, n := range nodes {\n\t\tif n.Type != \"code.Call\" || n.Prop(\"callee_path\") != \"analysis.function.context.end\" {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tendCalls++\n\t\targs := n.Prop(\"str_args\")\n\t\tif len(args) > pyModuleLiteralMaxBytes+pyContextBaseTokenLimit*64 {\n\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"end call str_args is %d bytes; the module literal context must be bounded at %d\", len(args), pyModuleLiteralMaxBytes)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif strings.Contains(args, earlyMarker) {\n\t\t\twithEarly++\n\t\t}\n\t\tif strings.Contains(args, lateMarker) {\n\t\t\twithLate++\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif endCalls == 0 {\n\t\tt.Fatal(\"no analysis.function.context.end call was lowered\")\n\t}\n\tif withEarly != endCalls {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the earliest module literal is missing from %d of %d end calls; the bound keeps a prefix, not a sample\", endCalls-withEarly, endCalls)\n\t}\n\tif withLate != 0 {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the module literal context past the bound rides %d of %d end calls; a %d-byte literal mass must not ride every function\", withLate, endCalls, pyModuleLiteralMaxBytes)\n\t}\n}"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d3b39ce-4baf-4531-a837-11deefe45eb7","uuid":"591ae8e6-37a6-408e-9178-9feee0517326","timestamp":"2026-09-19T05:40:56.387Z"}
