{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260919134752e24d7aa62e46437a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The report format: findings with `taint path: <modkey>Call#21878 -> <modkey>Arg#21879` — the ordinals that shift when node counts change. Normalization: replace `#\\d+` with `#N` in taint paths. The previous session said outputs were \"byte-identical after normalising internal node ordinals\".\n\nNow write the parity harness: for each target, run base and fix through the mandated wrapper, normalize (`#\\d+` → `#N`), diff. Targets:\n1. openrazer (rank 2794's repo)\n2. /tmp/bench/{BenchmarkJava,BenchmarkPython,ports}\n3. All 66 RealVuln repos\n\nThe wrapper writes report to stdout (fix-owasp.out has the findings) — with rc=3 (exitCheckFail) when findings exist. Note peakrss python wrapper — for the sweep I don't need peakrss everywhere; but consistent timing is nice for openrazer. For the sweep, plain campaign-scan runs, capture stdout, normalize, diff.\n\nLet me write the harness script.","signature":"d5ae8f4cf56f4f418efe62d2"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d3b39ce-4baf-4531-a837-11deefe45eb7","uuid":"4537899b-4e24-4172-92fd-ff9f89f4f94a","timestamp":"2026-09-19T05:48:01.036Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260919134752e24d7aa62e46437a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_9dacf63186e04bc1a0aa2780","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/parity.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Parity harness: scan each target with base and fix binaries through the\nmandated campaign-scan wrapper, normalise node ordinals (#123 -> #N) in taint\npaths, and diff the reports.\"\"\"\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nDATA = \"/campaign/repos/defs/vyql\"\nORD = re.compile(r\"#\\d+\")\n\n\ndef run(binary: str, target: str, out: Path) -> str:\n    r = subprocess.run(\n        [\"campaign-scan\", target, \"--data-dir\", DATA, \"--binary\", binary],\n        capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=600, cwd=str(out.parent),\n    )\n    (out.parent / out.name).with_suffix(\".rc\").write_text(str(r.returncode))\n    return r.stdout\n\n\ndef normalise(text: str) -> str:\n    return ORD.sub(\"#N\", text)\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    base, fix = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]\n    targets = [Path(p).resolve() for p in sys.argv[3:]]\n    workdir = Path(\"/tmp/parity\")\n    workdir.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n    diffs, errors = [], []\n    for t in targets:\n        name = t.name\n        try:\n            b = normalise(run(base, str(t), workdir / f\"{name}.base\"))\n            f = normalise(run(fix, str(t), workdir / f\"{name}.fix\"))\n        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n            errors.append((name, \"timeout\"))\n            continue\n        (workdir / f\"{name}.base\").write_text(b)\n        (workdir / f\"{name}.fix\").write_text(f)\n        if b == f:\n            print(f\"IDENTICAL {name} ({len(b)} bytes)\")\n        else:\n            import difflib\n            d = list(difflib.unified_diff(b.splitlines(), f.splitlines(), lineterm=\"\", n=1))\n            (workdir / f\"{name}.diff\").write_text(\"\\n\".join(d[:400]))\n            diffs.append((name, len(d)))\n            print(f\"DIFF     {name}: {len(d)} diff lines\")\n    print(f\"\\n{len(targets)-len(diffs)-len(errors)}/{len(targets)} identical, \"\n          f\"{len(diffs)} diff, {len(errors)} error\")\n    for name, n in diffs:\n        print(f\"  diff: {name} ({n} lines) -> /tmp/parity/{name}.diff\")\n    for name, why in errors:\n        print(f\"  error: {name}: {why}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d3b39ce-4baf-4531-a837-11deefe45eb7","uuid":"5ee2776d-2c5b-4001-b75d-77515afc1c0f","timestamp":"2026-09-19T05:48:05.823Z"}
