{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2026091913561597a42616777249ee","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No `args.count` predicates on analysis.* paths — all on real library calls. Safe.\n\nNext concern: **NIR golden fixtures**. Are there golden files pinning the NIR of Python files (which would show the args change)? The full suite passed, so if goldens exist they passed — either they don't cover the context calls or they were updated... they passed, that's what matters.\n\nAnother check: **js/ruby/php/csharp/elixir frontends** have their own function-context emitters — do they carry a moduleContext analogue? The task is Python-specific; other frontends unchanged (their scans' node counts unchanged → their findings' ordinals unchanged). My change only touches the Python converter. ✓.\n\nNow, while tasks run — start drafting the verdict. Also think about what remains:\n\n1. ✅ Rework commits (3): drop sweep artifacts, merge main, literal economy.\n2. ✅ Failing tests at base (3 new, proven).\n3. ✅ Full suite fix tree green (rc=0, 30 pkgs).\n4. ⏳ Specs count (running).\n5. ⏳ Base suite (running — expect green).\n6. ⏳ RealVuln sweep (running).\n7. ✅ openrazer: base rc=1 empty (3.38GB) vs fix rc=3 208 findings (770MB, 7.1s); my delta finding-identical to HEAD.\n8. ✅ Bench corpora identical vs current main.\n9. ✅ dense3: main/mb/HEAD die at stop; full fix completes 67s/1.7GB. densepy: base dies at stop; full fix rc=124 timeout at 12×2000 (documented residual).\n10. Push branch, restore harness files, write verdict.\n\nThe densepy residual — let me reconsider ONE more time whether to leave it. The gap's mandate: \"under the mandated 4GB cap and 180 second timeout the repository scan writes an empty report\" — the fix must let the repository-level proof be produced. For the rank's repo (openrazer): done, with 4× memory margin and 25× time margin. For synthetic dense corpora: dense3 done (6000 funcs). densepy (2