{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202609191359003bc2dc32c44e44d3","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confusing: `gh api repos/vyprai/vyql --jq .permissions` says push:true, maintain:true, admin:true for kikihakiem?! But git push over https got 403. The credentials file has two entries: `https://x-access-token:...` and `https://vypr:...` — maybe the git credential helper offered the WRONG credential (vypr's) or the x-access-token expired, while GH_TOKEN works for API.\n\nTry pushing with the token explicitly: use GH_TOKEN as the git credential (git push with URL embedding, or `gh` as credential helper): `git -c credential.helper='!gh auth git-credential' push origin ...`.","signature":"9ead4cbbff1e4a24b8bc0b23"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d3b39ce-4baf-4531-a837-11deefe45eb7","uuid":"ba1c43cc-47fa-42a0-b4c5-a9dec566a8ad","timestamp":"2026-09-19T05:59:05.164Z"}
