any.literal contains` → substring containment over call `str_args` (bindings_value.go, `valCondsFoldedNeedles` etc.); presence predicates walk Const nodes; binding needles anchored on module facts use `callee.analysis == \"function.context.end\"`.\n   - Token conventions: `pyContextCompact` bounds per-literal token contribution at 160 bytes (longer literal → no token); literals >160B cannot leak via `module_literal:` tokens.\n   - `campaign-scan` = `timeout 180 vyql scan -data <dir> --max-ram 4GB --cache off <target>`; data dir `/campaign/repos/defs/vyql`.\n   - Test protocol: `CGO_ENABLED=1 VYQL_HOME=/campaign/repos/defs/vyql go test -count=1 ./...`.\n   - Memory safety stop: scan aborts at 3.3 GiB resident under `-max-ram 4GB` with empty report, rc=1.\n   - Partitioning: `PlanPartitions` splits big targets; per-partition in-RAM store.\n   - Ordinal normalization for output parity: `#\\d+` → `#N` (taint-path node ordinals shift with node-count changes).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/campaign/work/engine-the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan.task.json` — the gap definition (read-only).\n   - `internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/python.go` — core fix (commit 9243083fac):\n     - `pyFunctionContext`: removed `nir.Const{Loc: loc, Value: c.moduleContext}` from the shared `args` slice (now only lang/name/bodyText/compact); after `endArgs := append([]nir.Expr(nil), args...)` added:\n     ```go\n     if c.moduleContext != \"\" {\n         endArgs = append(endArgs, nir.Const{Loc: endLoc, Value: c.moduleContext})\n     }\n     if len(c.moduleTokens) > 0 {\n         endArgs = append(endArgs, nir.Const{\n             Loc:   endLoc,\n             Value: \"module_\" + strings.Join(c.moduleTokens, \"\\x00module_\"),\n         })\n     }\n     ```\n     (with a long explanatory comment: module literal context and tokens ride the `.end` call ALONE; bindings asking for module facts anchor on `callee.analysis == \"function.context.end\"`).\n     - `pyModuleLiteralContext` bounded:\n     ```go\n     func (c *pyConv) pyModuleLiteralContext(root *tree_sitter.Node) string {\n         var toks []string\n         kept := 0\n         var walk func(n *tree_sitter.Node)\n         walk = func(n *tree_sitter.Node) {\n             if n == nil || kept >= pyModuleLiteralMaxBytes {\n                 return\n             }\n             if c.kind(n) == \"string\" || c.kind(n) == \"concatenated_string\" {\n                 text := c.text(n)\n                 kept += len(text) + 1\n                 toks = append(toks, text)\n                 return\n             }\n             for _, ch := range c.namedChildren(n) {\n                 walk(ch)\n             }\n         }\n         walk(root)\n         return strings.Join(toks, \"\\n\")\n     }\n     ```\n     (with doc comment: bounded at pyModuleLiteralMaxBytes; source-order prefix; every module smaller than it is joined whole).\n   - `internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/python_context_control.go` — added constant to the existing const block:\n     ```go\n     // pyModuleLiteralMaxBytes bounds the module literal context (see\n     // pyModuleLiteralContext): ...\n     pyModuleLiteralMaxBytes = 64 << 10\n     ```\n   - `internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/python_context_economy_test.go` — three new tests (plus the two from 7ea095b889 which still pass): `TestPythonModuleLiteralContextRidesTheEndCallAlone` (marker `zz_module_literal_marker_zz` at module scope; end calls must carry it, non-end context calls must not; fails at base with \"6 non-end context calls carry the module's literal context\"); `TestPythonManyFunctionModuleLiteralJoinBudget` (400 funcs; sums `len(n.StrArgs)` over the three non-end context paths; `const budget = funcs * 3 * (2 << 10)`; fails at base with \"1200 non-end context calls joined 26012820 bytes\"); `TestPythonModuleLiteralContextIsBounded` (200 × 1KB literals + early marker + >160B late marker `zz_late_ + 256 y's`; asserts end str_args ≤ `(64<<10)+py