{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202609191402363367710eaa6b4dc9","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_640d1f06240e48778f70687d","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/campaign/work/engine-the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan.answer.json","content":"{\n  \"gap\": \"the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan\",\n  \"status\": \"DONE\",\n  \"commit\": \"9243083fac57c5c3131a049396f6768dc0cc167b\",\n  \"commits\": [\n    \"31d5f496e3978c99ed91893c6cc388735759fe90\",\n    \"c169eaeb0bed44f1063f233d4c93e2da07f0d853\",\n    \"7ea095b88962eb97a721fe825322fbfeec2fb836\",\n    \"bab388bd97cebf7ee3fcc0c71db03b68298ace1e\",\n    \"964c8e7952f95144bce57e1c60c78d55fc3337bc\",\n    \"9243083fac57c5c3131a049396f6768dc0cc167b\"\n  ],\n  \"branch\": \"engine-work/the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan\",\n  \"base\": \"f24ca8032054175bc4d04b2098567242e541dca2\",\n  \"changed_files\": [\n    \"cmd/vyql/main.go\",\n    \"cmd/vyql/maxram_test.go\",\n    \"internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/python.go\",\n    \"internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/python_context_control.go\",\n    \"internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/python_context_economy_test.go\"\n  ],\n  \"blocked_ranks\": [\n    2794\n  ],\n  \"what_was_missing\": \"Two quadratic re-carriage terms in the Python frontend made the graph for dense multi-package Python code quadratic in functions-per-module, pushing the mandated scan (-max-ram 4GB, timeout 180) over the engine's 3.3 GiB memory safety stop during lowering/graph construction — the scan aborted before any finding was emitted and wrote an empty repository report, so no rule could produce its repository-level proof. internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/python.go, (*pyConv).pyFunctionContext emits five synthetic analysis.* calls per Python function (context.source, context, context.sink, context.end, local.end), and each carried module-level facts per function: (1) the module's structured context tokens (c.moduleTokens, capped at pyContextBaseTokenLimit = 512) as one Const argument PER TOKEN on the end call — closed by 7ea095b889, which joins them into one Const; (2) the module's RAW literal context (c.moduleContext = pyModuleLiteralContext = every string literal in the module joined) riding FOUR of the five calls, with lowering (internal/extract/lowering/lowering.go, (*lowerer).evalCall) re-joining each call's literals into str_args — 4 x F x L bytes of joins and Const payloads for a module of F functions and L bytes of literals — closed by 9243083fac, which moves it to the end call alone and bounds it at pyModuleLiteralMaxBytes = 64KiB (source-order prefix). Measured at current main f24ca80320: a scratch profile of one 2000-function file attributed 3,171 MiB of str_args and 1,153 MiB of lit4 props to this one term; the mandated campaign-scan of /tmp/dense3 (3 x 2000 functions) exits rc=1 at 3,432,748 kB peak RSS with 'the scan reached 3.3 GiB of resident memory, at the safety threshold below -max-ram 4GB; stopping' and an empty report; and rank 2794's own repository, openrazer at /campaign/work/rank-2794-1/repo, NOW DIES THE SAME WAY at main: rc=1, peak 3,382,580 kB, empty report (the merge-base 522a598a1d binary also stops: same message). The prior session's fix (7ea095b889, joined tokens) was necessary but no longer sufficient for openrazer after main moved underneath it — re-measured this session, HEAD without the literal change completes openrazer at 1.9 GB but the literal term still killed the synthetic dense corpora; with it, everything below fits.\",\n  \"what_changed\": \"Three code commits across two sessions, one behaviour; plus three branch-hygiene commits that carry no net diff. 31d5f496e3: cmd/vyql/main.go holdOneGraphInRAM keeps a one-graph bounded scan's store in RAM when the configured ceiling fits the estimated graph (removes the disk store's resident overhead); necessary, not sufficient. 7ea095b889: pyFunctionContext's end call carries the module token re-carriage as ONE joined Const ('module_' + strings.Join(c.moduleTokens, '\\\\x00module_')) instead of one Const per token; value matching reads the same bytes and the presence predicates split on the same \\\\x00, so matching is unchanged, only node count (a 400-function module lowers to 300 nodes per function instead of 1322). 9243083fac: (a) the module literal context Const is removed from the shared args slice and appended to endArgs only, so analysis.function.context.end alone carries it — bindings asking for module facts already anchor there (callee.analysis == 'function.context.end'), so every literal stays reachable while the 4 x F x L join term collapses to F x L(min, 64KiB); (b) pyModuleLiteralContext is bounded at pyModuleLiteralMaxBytes = 64 << 10 (source-order prefix; every module smaller than the bound is joined whole — measured, the largest real-corpus module is 55 KiB, so no real module loses a byte). Hygiene: c169eaeb0b is the campaign sweep's commit of left-uncommitted work and bab388bd97 drops the run artifacts (harness.err/harness.log/telemetry.json) that same sweep put on the branch — net zero together; 964c8e7952 merges main f24ca80320 in. Net PR diff vs origin/main: exactly the five files listed, all inside cmd/ and internal/.\",\n  \"test\": \"internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/python_context_economy_test.go, five tests. The two from 7ea095b889 (TestPythonFunctionEndModuleTokensAreOneLiteral, TestPythonManyFunctionModuleGraphBudget) pin the joined-token shape and the <=500-nodes-per-function graph budget. The three new ones from 9243083fac, each verified FAILING on the pre-change tree (origin/main f24ca80320, test file applied there) and PASSING at 9243083fac: TestPythonModuleLiteralContextRidesTheEndCallAlone — module-scope marker 'zz_module_literal_marker_zz' must appear on every end call's str_args and on NO non-end context call's (base failure: '6 non-end context calls carry the module's literal context'); TestPythonManyFunctionModuleLiteralJoinBudget — 400 functions x 3 non-end context calls must join < 400 x 3 x 2KiB of literal bytes (base failure: '1200 non-end context calls joined 26012820 bytes'); TestPythonModuleLiteralContextIsBounded — 200 x 1KiB module literals: every end call's str_args must stay <= 64KiB + 512 x 64B, an early marker present on all end calls and a >160B late marker (beyond the token path's per-literal cap) absent past the bound (base failure: 'end call str_args is 211786 bytes'; assertions inline 64 << 10 so the file compiles at base). Also cmd/vyql/maxram_test.go pins holdOneGraphInRAM's store choice. Suite state: CGO_ENABLED=1 VYQL_HOME=/campaign/repos/defs/vyql go test -count=1 ./... rc=0, 30 packages ok, at HEAD and at the base tree; TestVyqlSpecs verbose 10,395 subtests PASS, 0 FAIL; gofmt and go vet clean.\",\n  \"verification\": \"All runs through the mandated `campaign-scan <target> --data-dir /campaign/repos/defs/vyql` (timeout 180, --max-ram 4GB, --cache off carried by the wrapper). base = binary built from origin/main f24ca80320; fix = binary built from HEAD 9243083fac; taint-path node ordinals normalised (#\\\\d+ -> #N) before diffing, because node counts change by design. (1) Blocked rank's repository — openrazer (/campaign/work/rank-2794-1/repo): base rc=1, peak 3,382,580 kB, EMPTY report, stop message; merge-base binary same; fix rc=3 (check ran, exitCheckFail), peak 770,084 kB, 7.1s, 208 findings. (2) Reproducer corpora: /tmp/dense3 (3 files x 2000 functions): base rc=1 at 3,432,748 kB empty; fix rc=0, peak 1,707,360 kB, 66.9s, report written. /tmp/scale500: base rc=1 at 3,432,748 kB; fix rc=0, 2,603,488 kB. /tmp/nolit (dense, literal-free control): fix rc=0, 1,184,824 kB — isolates the literal term. /tmp/densepy (12 x 2000): base rc=1 empty; fix rc=124 timeout at 180s with peak only 1.88 GB (memory solved; 12 partitions x ~22s exceeds the wall clock — documented residual, no real corpus is near it: the heaviest real corpus, realvuln-owasp-web-playground, scans in 1.4s / 131,572 kB / 41 findings). (3) The 9243083fac change alone is finding-neutral: the HEAD-without-it binary (964c8e7952) completes openrazer byte-identically to the full fix after ordinal normalisation. (4) Bench corpora byte-identical vs main (no normalisation needed): BenchmarkJava 11,293,639 B, BenchmarkPython 3,429,306 B, ports 5,770,686 B. (5) Full Real-Vuln corpus (66 repos, mandated wrapper): every repo's finding count identical base vs fix (total 3498 = 3498); 62/66 outputs identical after ordinal normalisation; lets-be-bad-guys 226 = 226 findings with identical header/advisory multisets (pure tie reorder from shifted node ids); three vc-*-django repos flip one CSRF finding's evidence anchor between 'analysis.parameter.entry is marked csrf-exempt' and 'analysis.function.context is marked csrf-exempt' (same finding, rule, location, severity, confidence — one line each).\",\n  \"blast_radius\": \"Every Python-containing scan's graph gets smaller and its node ordinals shift; anything pinning exact ordinals in output sees the shift (reports use #N-class labels in taint paths, which is why the parity harness normalises them). Zero finding-count movement anywhere measured: 10,395 spec subtests identical, openrazer 208 = 208 (and now completes instead of dying), three bench corpora byte-identical, 66-repo RealVuln corpus 3498 = 3498 with 62 byte-identical after normalisation and the 4 named text-only deltas (one tie reorder, three one-line evidence-anchor flips). Memory is uniformly lower (openrazer from over-the-stop to 770 MB; bench corpora a few percent; dense corpora from 3.4 GB death to 1.7-2.6 GB completion). Non-Python frontends untouched. The change is inert for modules with no string literals and for modules whose literal mass is under 64KiB (joined whole, byte-identical) — which measurement says covers every real corpus module.\",\n  \"considered_and_rejected\": [\n    \"Fixing it in lowering (skip minting Const+Arg for literal args of analysis.* calls) — tried on the first attempt, broke 35 TestVyqlSpecs subtests: the synthetic Consts ARE the per-function fact carriers for presence predicates. The economy belongs where the facts are shaped, in the frontend.\",\n    \"Dropping the end-call re-carriage entirely and letting analysis.module.context carry module facts alone — the per-function carriage is load-bearing (presence scopes are per function; python_context_test.go pins module_ tokens on each function's end call). Removing it changes which findings fire, not just their cost.\",\n\n    \"A module literal budget below 64KiB — would truncate the largest real module (mouse.py-class files measure up to 55KiB) and change findings on real corpora; 64KiB keeps every measured real module byte-identical.\",\n    \"A literal-count cap (512 literals) as the primary bound — byte budget is the honest currency (the cost is bytes joined, not literal count) and a count cap would clip many-small-literal modules that are cheap anyway.\",\n    \"Raising the memory stop or the ceiling, or the timeout — the 4GB/180s policy is campaign-mandated; the gap is the engine's graph being too big for it.\",\n\n    \"The store-side fix alone (31d5f496e3) — measured insufficient: dense corpora still died at the stop with it.\"\n  ],\n  \"reviewer_should_know\": \"The gap now reproduces on the blocked rank's OWN repository at main (openrazer: rc=1, empty report, 3.38 GB) and the reworked branch scans it to a full 208-finding report in 7.1s at 770 MB — that is the headline. Known residuals, both stated rather than hidden: (a) /tmp/densepy (12 files x 2000 functions, synthetic) now completes each partition in ~22s but 12 partitions exceed the 180s wall clock — a partitioning/throughput limit, not the memory-safety stop the gap names, and four orders of magnitude past the heaviest real corpus (1.4s); (b) the 64KiB literal bound is a real behavioural bound — a module with >64KiB of literals keeps a source-order prefix on the end call (every token under 160B is still separately reachable via module_literal: tokens, so the marker path degrades gracefully). Environment blocker, verbatim: publishing the branch from this worktree fails — `git push origin engine-work/the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan` -> 'remote: Permission to vyprai/vyql.git denied to kikihakiem. fatal: unable to access https://github.com/vyprai/vyql.git/: The requested URL returned error: 403' — for every available credential (plain push, gh auth git-credential, and the stored vypr credential as explicit Authorization header), while `gh api repos/vyprai/vyql --jq .permissions` reports push:true for the authenticated user; looks like proxy-level auth rewriting. The branch is committed locally at 9243083fac (all six commits); the remote branch still points at 7ea095b889 and PR #242 therefore shows the old head — the campaign side must fast-forward it, same as it published the earlier commits. harness.err and harness.log remain untracked dirt in the worktree (live harness output, not mine); the tracked tree is clean at 9243083fac.\",\n  \"engine_gap\": null\n}\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d3b39ce-4baf-4531-a837-11deefe45eb7","uuid":"5b133913-cecd-4a3a-8b80-e69d7bca66ce","timestamp":"2026-09-19T06:03:21.042Z"}
