{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2026091914033225da7051f8634f34","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_500d1642adad4941965abe8f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/campaign/work/engine-the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan/.claude/projects/-campaign-repos-engine/memory/git-push-403-campaign-publishes.md","content":"---\nname: git-push-403-campaign-publishes\ndescription: git push from engine worktrees is 403-denied for every local credential; the campaign side publishes branches — don't retry pushes\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n`git push origin <branch>` from an engine worktree fails with `remote: Permission to vyprai/vyql.git denied to kikihakiem` / HTTP 403 for ALL available credentials (plain push, `gh auth git-credential`, the stored `vypr` credential as an explicit Authorization header), even though `gh api repos/vyprai/vyql --jq .permissions` reports `push:true`. Likely proxy-level auth rewriting.\n\n**Why:** Observed 2026-09-19 on the memory-safety-stop branch: three push strategies all 403'd, yet the campaign had previously published earlier commits of the same branch to the remote and opened PR #242 itself.\n\n**How to apply:** Commit the branch locally, state the commit SHA and the verbatim push error under `reviewer_should_know` in the verdict, and let the campaign fast-forward the remote/PR. Do not spend attempts on more credential variants. Related: [[harness-sweep-commits-dirt]].\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d3b39ce-4baf-4531-a837-11deefe45eb7","uuid":"faf9f228-1ebe-4053-b827-dd4e69ec1ddd","timestamp":"2026-09-19T06:03:38.910Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_500d1642adad4941965abe8f","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /campaign/work/engine-the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan/.claude/projects/-campaign-repos-engine/memory/git-push-403-campaign-publishes.md"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d3b39ce-4baf-4531-a837-11deefe45eb7","uuid":"63e3182b-5453-4ee2-866d-d3f8cb8256af","timestamp":"2026-09-19T06:03:38.924Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/campaign/work/engine-the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan/.claude/projects/-campaign-repos-engine/memory/git-push-403-campaign-publishes.md","content":"---\nname: git-push-403-campaign-publishes\ndescription: \"git push from engine worktrees is 403-denied for every local credential; the campaign side publishes branches — don't retry pushes\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 3d3b39ce-4baf-4531-a837-11deefe45eb7\n  modified: 2026-09-19T06:03:38.915Z\n---\n\n`git push origin <branch>` from an engine worktree fails with `remote: Permission to vyprai/vyql.git denied to kikihakiem` / HTTP 403 for ALL available credentials (plain push, `gh auth git-credential`, the stored `vypr` credential as an explicit Authorization header), even though `gh api repos/vyprai/vyql --jq .permissions` reports `push:true`. Likely proxy-level auth rewriting.\n\n**Why:** Observed 2026-09-19 on the memory-safety-stop branch: three push strategies all 403'd, yet the campaign had previously published earlier commits of the same branch to the remote and opened PR #242 itself.\n\n**How to apply:** Commit the branch locally, state the commit SHA and the verbatim push error under `reviewer_should_know` in the verdict, and let the campaign fast-forward the remote/PR. Do not spend attempts on more credential variants. Related: [[harness-sweep-commits-dirt]].\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false,"memdirStamped":true}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2026091914033225da7051f8634f34","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_60ee2ca9dc2746b6b9cfc0cf","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/campaign/work/engine-the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan/.claude/projects/-campaign-repos-engine/memory/harness-sweep-commits-dirt.md","content":"---\nname: harness-sweep-commits-dirt\ndescription: The campaign sweep auto-commits uncommitted worktree files (incl. live harness.err/harness.log/telemetry.json) onto engine branches as out-of-lane commits\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nA periodic campaign sweep commits whatever is left uncommitted in an engine worktree — including live harness output (`harness.err`, `harness.log`, `telemetry.json`) and scratch files — as an out-of-lane commit on the branch (observed: `c169eaeb0b \"engine <gap>: commit the work left uncommitted\"` carrying CHANGELOG.md + harness files + telemetry.json).\n\n**Why:** Out-of-lane files in the PR diff can get a rework refused; on the memory-safety-stop branch this cost a cleanup commit (`bab388bd97 \"engine: drop the run artifacts the sweep committed onto this branch\"`).\n\n**How to apply:** Before going idle, leave the tracked tree clean (commit real work, delete scratch) and delete/ignore run artifacts; `harness.err`/`harness.log` reappear as untracked live-harness output and are expected dirt — name them in the verdict rather than committing them. If a sweep commit already landed, revert its out-of-lane payload with an explicit drop commit rather than rewriting history. Related: [[git-push-403-campaign-publishes]].\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d3b39ce-4baf-4531-a837-11deefe45eb7","uuid":"3bc4ac7e-1c31-45c6-ae75-075e99a8206e","timestamp":"2026-09-19T06:03:43.099Z"}
